On Tue, Jul 30, 2002 at 04:57:26AM +0000, Pavel Machek wrote:
> > Oops! 90° is way to hot; no wonder that the machine crashes.
> 
> No it is not. If it was too hot for correct operation, machine must 
> powerdown.

P4s only trip (power-down) at 135C.  They only start throttling at 85C.
This means 90C is too hot for normal operation, by definition. :)

